Z||000000||hercules||01-06-2000||11:53 AM||||Can anybody tell me what size the factory speakers are in the dashboard and behind the seats?  I am replacing the whole stereo system and want to make sure I get the right size speakers.  I have an '86 GT Fastback if that helps.  Thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000001||HF6582||01-06-2000||12:05 PM||||They are 4x10 in the dash and 4x6 in the sail panels.<P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||hercules||01-06-2000||12:12 PM||||Great, thanks for your help!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||x cuda man||01-06-2000||12:19 PM||||hercules,the fronts are 4x10's and the rear is 4x6's,check out fierosound's web page, the system he's got is THE BOMB!this is the way to "rock down" in a fiero! he's got a little bit different set up in the front.find it at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierosound</A>   (also, is there anybody out there that can tell us if there's any better 4x10's than the pioneer 2 and 3way's with the paper cone's? thanks<p>[This message has been edited by x cuda man (edited 01-06-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||Dave85||01-06-2000||12:46 PM||||Kenwood and Alpine make 4x10's but they are 2-way. They sound pretty good. I think the Pioneer 3-ways may actually be better. I am planning to put Pioneer 6x9's #6999 up front. These are suposed to be awsome!<BR>As far as 4x6 go, I think the Kenwood eXcelon is probably the best.<BR>Now, for the best prices. The best place I've found (without joining a wholesale club) is Autotoys.com.<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ditz88GT||01-06-2000||05:32 PM||||I just bought Kicker 4"X10"'s and they rock.  I've had the Pioneers, and they are better than stock but not much.  I plan on replacing the back speakers with the Kicker 4"X6"'s as soon as I can too.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Tom88gt||01-06-2000||06:21 PM||||Whatever you do, make sure the front and rear speakers are the same brand and type.  Otherwise it may sound "off" and distracting.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Richard Parnell||01-06-2000||08:28 PM||||I'm changing the front speakers in my car and when looking at the factory speakers in the car, I noticed they are 10 Ohm as opposed to the new 8 Ohmers I just got.  Is there a problem ?  Shouldn't be, right?||||reg||5
Z||000008||Dave85||01-06-2000||09:17 PM||||Ditz, <BR>Do you have the specs on those Kickers. What's the frequency response?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||01-06-2000||11:05 PM||||The difference between 8 ohm and 10 ohm should not be noticeable. GM will sometimes juggle the impedences to get a different balance. Had a Firebird that came with 8 ohm speakers in the front, and 4 ohm speakers in the back. ||||reg||1
